post_install() {
    cat <<'EOF'

OpenKingdoms is the engine only. It ships no game content.

To play you need your own copy of Total Annihilation: Kingdoms, from the GOG
"Total Annihilation Commander Pack" or the original CDs. The engine reads the
.hpi archives from that install directly and never copies them.

Point it at your copy once:

    openkingdoms --game-dir "/path/to/Total Annihilation Kingdoms"

or export TAK_GAME_DIR, or put the game in a folder called "game" beside the
binary. The folder is remembered afterwards, so this is asked once.

Settings and saved games go to ~/.local/share/OpenKingdoms/OpenKingdoms/.

Skirmish against the AI and multiplayer are playable. The campaign is not
finished yet: some missions cannot be completed and campaign progress is not
written to disk.

EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
    post_install
}
